-- title:
--   Finite-part m-torsion counted by A-sections of the m-kernel
-- statement:
--   Fix natural numbers $N_0$ and $p$ with $N_0 \neq 0$ and $p$ prime, and assume $p \nmid N_0$. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of an algebraic closure of $\mathbf{Q}$ satisfying `A.LiesOverPrime p`, i.e. the image of $p$ in the ambient field lies in the nonunits of $A$; let $\Lambda$ be a level datum `LevelData N₀ p A`, which provides in particular a morphism $\sigma_A : \operatorname{Spec} A \to \mathrm{base}\ p$ compatible with the generic point, together with a scheme over $\mathrm{base}\ p$ carrying a relative group law and dictionaries of points at level $N_0$; and let $O$ be an object of `JZeroNeronObjectAtP N₀ p hpN₀ A hA Λ`, so that $O$ consists of a scheme $G$ with structure morphism $g$ to $\mathrm{base}\ p$, a commutative relative group law `O.L` on $g$, a bijection `O.pts` from $J_0(N_0p)$ to the sections of $g$ over the generic point, and the geometric and arithmetic hypotheses recorded in that structure (smoothness, separatedness, local finite type, quasi-compactness, surjectivity, preconnected fibres, additivity and Galois equivariance of `O.pts`, Hecke compatibility, flatness and surjectivity of multiplication by $n$ for $n > 0$, properness of the generic fibre, the toric rank and the remaining fields), summarised here. Then for every $m : \mathbb{N}$ the number of elements of the additive subgroup `O.finPts m` of $J_0(N_0p)$ — generated by those $x$ lying in `jZeroTorsion (N₀ * p) m` and satisfying `ExtendsToPlace A Λ.σA (O.pts x)` — equals the number of morphisms $s : \operatorname{Spec} A \to (\mathtt{O.L.baseChange }\Lambda.\sigma_A).\mathrm{schemeKer}\ m$ with $s$ followed by `schemeKerStr m` equal to the identity; here the base-changed group law is the relative group law on $g$ pulled back along $\sigma_A$, its $m$-kernel is the pullback of multiplication by $m$ along the unit section, and `schemeKerStr m` is the second projection of that pullback, so the morphisms counted are exactly the sections of the $m$-kernel over $\operatorname{Spec} A$.
--
--   This is the dictionary step identifying the finite-part $m$-torsion subgroup of $J_0(N_0p)$, defined through extension of points to the valuation ring $A$, with the group of $A$-valued sections of the scheme-theoretic $m$-kernel of the base-changed relative group law. It feeds the computation of the cardinality of `finPts` in [`ModularCurve.JZeroNeronObjectAtP.natCard_finPts`](thm.html#ModularCurve.JZeroNeronObjectAtP.natCard_finPts), and uses the membership criterion [`ModularCurve.JZeroNeronObjectAtP.mem_finPts_iff`](thm.html#ModularCurve.JZeroNeronObjectAtP.mem_finPts_iff).
